// Pattern knob table: ONE row per BulletSpawner2D "Bullet Patterns" property,
// in inspector (and .tscn) order. Expanded by X-macros into the spawner
// accessors and their validation (bullet_spawner2d_pattern_properties.cpp),
// the accessor declarations (bullet_spawner2d.hpp), the ClassDB binds
// (bullet_spawner2d_bindings.cpp) and the by-name knob writer of
// BulletPatterns2D.generate (pattern_knob_access2d.cpp).
//
// PATTERN_SUBGROUP(title, prefix)
// PATTERN_KNOB(param type, value type, Variant type, name,
//     check 1, a, b, message 1, check 2, a, b, message 2, notify, hint, hint string)
//   A table-driven knob: the setter rejects a value when a check fails
//   ("BulletSpawner2D: <name> <message>, keeping the old value.") and
//   otherwise stores it, re-gates the inspector when notify is true, and
//   calls on_pattern_changed(). Checks: PatternKnobCheck2D (patterns/
//   pattern_knob_checks2d.hpp).
// PATTERN_PROPERTY(Variant type, name, hint, hint string, setter, getter)
//   A property of the group whose accessors are hand-written (node paths,
//   arrays, enum-typed Path2D knobs, spawner-owned settings).
//
// SCENE COMPAT: names are serialized. Never rename a row; reordering rows
// reorders the inspector and the saved .tscn lines (harmless, but noisy).

PATTERN_PROPERTY(INT, pattern_source, PROPERTY_HINT_ENUM, pattern_source_hint(), set_pattern_source, get_pattern_source)
